 # Changelog
 
+## S306p REVIEW 88'S FINDINGS ON THE QUEUE'S CODE, AND M61'S (the framework's thin path, T7b part 1; P-885; B2018) (2026-11-27)
+
+- **The rerun (`scripts/queue/rerun.py`), rebuilt (M62, M64 items 1 to 7, M65):** seat code runs as the unprivileged user
+  nobody, owning only its temporary directory, inside a network namespace; the wrap is trusted only once a probe inside it
+  sees no interface but the loopback and fails to write into a directory the runner owns; where no such wrap works no seat
+  code runs, and the card is HEAVY for the author's machine. The commit's files are written from their blobs, so
+  `.gitattributes` cannot change what runs, and the decisive script's hash is checked on the file as written; a symlinked
+  script, control or module is refused. The control's script is guarded as the decisive one is, and the guard refuses
+  `_socket`, `_ssl`, `ctypes`, `multiprocessing`, `logging.handlers`, `importlib`, `exec`, `eval`, `compile`, any use of
+  `__import__` and any change to `sys.path`. Every check that needs no run comes before HEAVY, and a failed run returns the
+  card before its control runs.
+- **The form (`card_form.py`; items 14, 18, 26, 28):** an effect names only codes the card touches; one table of codes (the
+  scoreboard in any case, identification and register rows, the law map's rows, the 19 by plural and common names); the
+  script's path stays in the commit and "run as" runs it; the control compared as a command; a line outside any field said;
+  hypotheses may hold ";"; the allowed packages read from ALLOWED_PACKAGES.json.
+- **The queue (`queue_schema.py`; items 9, 10, 19, 20, 27):** no card skips the peer offer; NOT_BANKED ends a card that
+  decides nothing, the runner's move; "main" on main's own card is that card's own seat; `deciding` true, false or null,
+  never 0 or 1; branches and times strict; strays and folders reported on a directory and on a ref.
+- **Discovery (`discover.py`; items 8, 12, 13, 19, 21, 22; M65):** a card's code is its branch's, from main's
+  queue/SEAT_CODES.json; its stated commit an ancestor of where it was found, with the same script and control there; a card
+  that cannot be filed is told to its seat and the others are filed; the vendor rule; `ls-tree -z`; fenced titles said;
+  versions keyed on branch, path and blob; a declared refile linked, the old version reported; a masked ref read only in
+  its mask; a masked Pins row read and an unreadable one reported, and a masked key of SEAT_CODES.json matched on the
+  rest, two matches refused (M66).
+- **Custody (`custody.py`; items 11, 23, 24):** a deleted card or log reported along the history; a log line of the wrong
+  kind said, never a stop; `--root`.
+- **The record check (`record_check.py`; items 15 to 17; M61):** "deciding" by the form's codes, the law map's rows among
+  them; the firewall's words widened; the retraction sweep loaded only where its registry stands; the title's words beyond
+  six said; a premise arc with its own card in the queue waited on until that card is VERIFIED.
+- **Tests:** 66 over the queue's six test files, a planted case for each item.
+
